'''Mountain trolls''' are [[aggressive]] creatures which can be found patrolling various mountainous areas. They are commonly killed as part of an assigned [[Slayer task]] of "[[trolls]]".

Trolls regenerate health twice as quickly as other monsters, but are still vulnerable to [[poison]]. They usually use [[crush weapons]], which, combined with their relatively high Strength, can hit rather hard. However, they attack slowly and are quite inaccurate, so it's not strictly necessary to use [[protection prayers]] for players that have high [[Defence]]. A good strategy for conserving supplies is to use [[Bones to Peaches]] on the big bones that they drop; this will almost always cover any damage they manage to deal. Bringing a [[staff of fire]] (or similar item) and [[Nature rune|nature runes]] is recommended in order to [[alchemy|alchemise]] their frequent low-level armour and weapon drops.

On [[Death Plateau (location)|Death Plateau]], they can be [[safespot]]ted from many areas; all of the stone fences and pretty much every other obstacle in the area can be shot over with [[Ranged]] or [[Magic]], however, they boast very high magic and ranged defence aside from attacks by [[standard ranged weapons]]. Wait to lose aggression so the Thrower Trolls no longer target you. [[Stick]] and [[Rock (Troll)|Rock]] count as mountain trolls and can easily be safespotted using the stone fence on the west side of the plateau for additional [[Slayer]] XP (beware that these two hit much harder and more often than standard mountain trolls). Alternatively, they can be safespotted around the corners of some rock piles in the [[Keldagrim]] entrance area.

Casting [[Monster Examine]] on a Mountain Troll is a task for the Kourend & Kebos Hard Achievement Diaries.

